course: dictionary
lesson: 4428
title: One small word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word hand has more than one meaning. To find out which one a writer means, look at the words around it. «Gran hands Sam a present» tells you Gran is giving something to Sam, so here hands is a verb: to hand something is to give it to someone with your hand.
explain: A hand is also a body part, the part at the end of your arm with four fingers and a thumb. «She breaks off a bit of the edge with each hand» uses hand this way. The clue is the word each: you have one hand on each side of your body.
explain: Some hand words have their own meanings. To give someone a hand means to help them. To hand out means to give one thing to each person. The hands of a clock are its pointers that show the time, so you need the words around them to tell which meaning is right.
fact: Hand can be a noun (a hand, hands) or a verb (to hand, handing).
fact: When you hand something to someone, you pass it to them, so they end up with more and you end up with less.
fact: The phrases «hand out», «hand in» and «hand over» each have their own meaning, so learn them as a group of words.
fact: British Sign Language (BSL) is a full language with its own grammar, and it uses hand shapes, movements, the face and the body.
exercise: «Gran hands Sam a present.» What does hands mean here? | *To give something with your hand | A pointer on a clock | A part of the body at the end of your arm | To help someone
exercise: «She breaks off a bit of the edge with each hand.» What is a hand in this sentence? | A pointer on a clock | *A part of the body at the end of your arm | A piece of paper | To give someone a present
exercise: Ella says, «Can you give me a hand with these bags?» What does she want? | Someone to hold her hand | A bag to carry | A clock to tell the time | *Help
test: What does hands mean in «a teacher hands Everett a note in front of everyone»? | Parts of the body at the end of the arm | *To give | Pointers on a clock | To help
test: What does «hand out» mean in «hand out the worksheets»? | Hide them under the desk | Take them away | *Give one to each person | Read them aloud
exam: Read «The King says the Cat may kiss his hand.» Which meaning of hand fits best? | To give something to someone | To help someone | *A part of the body at the end of an arm | A pointer that shows the time
